<figcaption>With a $1,000 bond, a 5% audit lottery makes any attack worth less than about $53 lose money. Without identity the attacker re-keys, B falls to zero, and the same $53 needs a 99.98% audit rate: full verification. Lines are safe-stake contours S* = c + (B + c)·p/(1−p), with c = 1¢; on these axes that exact relation is a straight line. Without the bond each unit of audit odds buys (B + c)/c ≈ 100,000 times less safe stake, so the odds must rise five decades. Moving up is free on the honest path; moving right is paid on every run.</figcaption>
</figure>
